+From abac2181a97967529e918d992560d9e0bf3937ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: zaldynbwtany202-dev
+ <227440178+zaldynbwtany202-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:46:41 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 1/4] gallery: price each voice in words, because tempo decides
+ what the text can keep
+
+Round three has a fixed budget - 1585 words over 632.5 s of original speech -
+and stretching is forbidden, so the candidate's measured pace is not a detail:
+it is how many words of meaning survive. voice-07 at 2.545 w/s, voice-13 at
+2.509 and voice-11 at 2.516 carry the whole rewrite and hand the leftover to
+breaths; at 2.17-2.35 w/s the ear gets a performance that must lose 60-145
+words. Recorded as data next to the clips so the cost is visible before the
+choice, not argued about after it.
+
+Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
