+Subject: [PATCH 4/4] The room tone this source offers is not room tone: refuse
+ it, and say why
+
+The acoustics match lifted its 'air' from dubs/.../source-analysis/vocal-pauses.json - and
+that file keeps the speech units under 'spans' and the breaths under 'pause_list'. Reading
+the wrong key laid the original narrator's own voice under our dub at -25.9 dBFS, with the
+same 215 Hz peak his voice has. The new provenance check catches it before any audio is
+written: pauses are chosen by shape, cross-checked against the ASR word cores, and the tile
+must sit at least 10 dB under typical speech and at or below the recording's own floor.
+
+It then refuses this source outright: the residual between the narrator's words measures
+9.8 dB below his speech level, because there is no silence here to steal - 655.99 s of
+speech in 676.33 s, 124 pauses averaging 0.161 s, and 63% of that 'pause' material still
+overlaps word cores. So --air-source none is now the honest default fallback: band and slope
+get matched, nothing gets added, and the report records the refusal and its numbers instead
+of hiding them.
+
+Two verification fixes found while certifying that render: the no-air path gets a stronger
+gate than spectral similarity (the delivered master must equal the filtered dry master to
+the sample, max_abs_difference <= 2e-4, so 'nothing was added' is proved, not assumed), and
+the lag search moved from np.correlate's quadratic loop - which stalled a run for twenty
+minutes - to an FFT over four seconds, after which the whole test file runs in 0.3 s.
+The correlation is left undefined-safe at 0.0 when the residual has no variance, so the
+published report never carries a NaN.
+
